RISKS
-The system could incorrectly identify a student as having completed or not completed their programme
-Unauthorised people could gain access to student records
-System could be down at anytime when students need their letter of completion
-Student records could be lost because of technical failures


ETHICAL CONSIDERATIONS
-Keep records of verification and letter-issuance decisions so they can be traced to authorised users.
-Protect digital letters from being falsely created, altered, or used by someone else.
-Allow authorised staff to review cases where the system cannot make a clear decision.
-Students should be able to understand their completion status and the reason for any rejection or delay.




